==Latin==
[[Image:The Chariot of Zeus - Project Gutenberg eText 14994.png|thumb|quadrīgae]]

===Etymology===
Contracted from {{term|quadriiugae|lang=la}}, feminine plural of {{term|quadriiugus||of or pertaining to a team of four|lang=la}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/kʷaˈdriː.ɡɛː/|lang=la}}
* {{audio|la-cls-quadrigae.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|quadrīgae|quadrigarum|quadrīgārum|f, pl|first}}

# A [[four]] [[horse]] [[team]], especially used for [[chariot]] [[racing]].
# {{poetic|lang=la}} The four-horse team drawing the chariot of the [[sun]].
# {{figurative}} [[free rein|Free rein]], free course.

